From: Neutron lab (team agent msi-rollback) 2026-11-08
Subject: [PATCH] msi: Roll back only what the failed install did to files, folders and component registration.

What was seen (lab, Adobe Acrobat Pro 26.002.22031, silent msiexec /i AcroPro.msi PATCH=AcrobatDCx64Upd2600222031.msp
in a copy of a prefix that already holds other Adobe apps; the install fails at PatchFiles, 1603): the rollback
deleted 261 files that were there before the install and that the install had left alone -- another app's
Linguistics/Hunspell files, Acrobat ActiveX, ARM, and the VC++ runtime DLLs in system32/syswow64.

Mechanism: Wine rolls back by re-running each standard action's inverse with every component and feature at its
pre-install state. InstallFiles' inverse, RemoveFiles, then deletes every file of every component whose pre-install
state is ABSENT -- which is the state of a component GUID registered to another product -- including files the
install kept because they were newer, the same version or a hash match. Files it overwrote were never saved. Brand
new components (state UNKNOWN) were skipped, so the files the install did create stayed (14 todo_wine checks in
tests/install.c). ProcessComponents' inverse recounted SharedDLLs per feature and could drop below the value from
before the install.

Windows behavior (Microsoft, "Rollback Installation"): while it runs the installation script the installer
"simultaneously generates a rollback script and saves a copy of every file deleted during the installation", keeps
those copies in a hidden system folder, deletes them after success, and on failure returns the system to its
original state.

Fix, the same structure: the install records what it does and rollback undoes only that.
- InstallFiles (cabinet and uncompressed paths) and PatchFiles record each target before writing it: missing ->
  rollback deletes it; existing -> a copy is saved to C:\Config.Msi and rollback moves it back. The first write
  to a path wins when several File rows target the same path. Files the install kept have no record and are left
  alone. Saved copies are deleted when the package is freed.
- create_folder() records each folder level it creates; rollback removes those, deepest first, only if empty.
- ProcessComponents records the component key (existed, this product's client value, permanent value) and every
  SharedDLLs value before writing them; rollback writes those values back instead of recounting.
- Rollback RemoveFiles no longer runs the RemoveFile table or deletes by component state.

Not covered (unchanged): registry values (RemoveRegistryValues by component state at rollback, same class of
problem), files deleted by the forward RemoveFiles/RemoveFile table (not saved), DuplicateFiles and MoveFiles,
GAC/WinSxS assemblies (with records, rollback no longer uninstalls them: a new one stays, a pre-existing one is no
longer removed), files replaced through the in-use/at-reboot path, rollback after REINSTALL (still skipped).
Restored files keep their contents; their times come back at 100 ns precision.

Test: tests/install.c test_rollback: product 1 installs a SharedDllRefCount component; product 2 shares it, creates
a file, finds an unversioned same-size file, a newer and an older versioned file, writes two paths twice, then a
deferred custom action (custom.dll rb_fail) fails. Checked: product 2 not registered, created file gone, the other
files byte-identical to before, SharedDLLs count still 1, product 1 still a client and product 2 not; uncompressed
and cabinet. The 14 todo_wine checks of failed installs (test_continuouscabs, test_caborder, test_missingcab,
test_sourcefolder) now pass and lose the marker.

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-185mr / 185amr = 185 / 185am + this msi.dll; tests cross-built with mingw):
- install tests: x86_64 4669 tests 0 failures, i386 4759 0 failures (n=2 each); kill switch on the same build:
  24 failures (n=2 each arch). The other 10 msi test files: same results as stock 185 on both arches.
- Acrobat case (fresh copies of the same base prefix, n=2): every one of 162199 pre-existing files still present,
  the 132 files the install had overwritten byte-identical to the base, no new file left under Acrobat DC, the
  shared component key back to its pre-install state. Kill switch on the same build (n=2): 261 files missing and
  the component left registered. SharedDLLs unchanged in all four runs.

Kill switch: NEUTRON_MSI_NO_ROLLBACK_RECORD=1 (previous behavior; read once per process).

